HCL's shape, in one example:

```hcl
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami           = data.aws_ami.latest.id
  instance_type = "t3.micro"
  tags = {
    Name = "web-${var.environment}"
  }
}
```

`resource "aws_instance" "web"` is a **block** — type, then a local name. Inside it, `ami = ...` is an **argument**. `data.aws_ami.latest.id` and `"web-${var.environment}"` are **expressions** — references and string interpolation resolved before any API call is made.

```hcl
resource "aws_security_group" "web_sg" {
  name = "web-sg"
  ingress {
    from_port = 443
    to_port   = 443
    protocol  = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami                    = data.aws_ami.latest.id
  instance_type          = "t3.micro"
  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.web_sg.id]
}
```

The instance references the security group's `id` — Terraform's graph sees that dependency and creates the security group first, with no ordering hint needed from you.
